  "goodToKnow": "Der Sumpf is a swamp or marsh: im Sumpf versinken. Figuratively, it's a morass of corruption or crime: den Sumpf trockenlegen (to drain the swamp). Much of northern Germany's wetland (Moor) was drained for farming, and today Moore are being rewetted to store carbon. Baron Münchhausen famously claimed to have pulled himself out of a swamp by his own hair. Sumpfig means marshy. Plural: die Sümpfe."
